# Level 5's own objects as the original runs them: levels 1 to 4 won at
# their frames 20, 30, 40 and 50 ($A07 and $A6C set, as a boss's payout
# does), so the game loads each next level as it would; the ship kept
# alive, still and firing, the shops skipped (as level-run.exp) but for
# level 5's end shop, which holds the game's ending ($1178C set), fire
# pressed every 30 s for each level's GET READY. Logged
# every frame ($3E42): the frame, the world line, fire, the ship, the random
# generator, the step ($CDA), the back limit ($CEA), the ship's box
# ($39252), the end boss's parts left ($D90), the level ($E1A), the level
# won ($A07) and the set speed ($CCC); every token taken ($4FF8), every
# enemy destroyed ($6250); and, on level 5, every update of an object of
# its own code as it starts (the snake $4F4DA, the pods $4F7A6 and their
# creatures $4FA1E, the three-part guns' ends $50E00, the wall guns $515DC,
# the turrets $5131E, the eight-way turrets $510A2, the mid boss $508E0, its
# turrets $507DA and its eye $506DE): its pc, object, type, x, y, +40, +48,
# hit points, +42, +44 and +62. For porting level 5's own code frame by
# frame.
# Run with --trace fdc.
expect prompt read sector sector=0x1 .*tr=0x0 .*addr=0x6760e
stage level2-jump.ini
stage level5-objs-start.ini
stage level5-frame.ini
stage weapons-take.ini
stage waves-kill.ini
stage level5-obj.ini
stage level-run-shield.ini
stage level-run-nodeath.ini
stage level-run-nowall.ini
stage level-run-noshop.ini
# Hatari 2.6 loses its breakpoints when a hit adds the 16th (it grows the
# array without copying it): grow it here, outside any hit, then clear it.
debug b pc = $1
debug b pc = $2
debug b pc = $3
debug b pc = $4
debug b pc = $5
debug b pc = $6
debug b pc = $7
debug b pc = $8
debug b pc = $9
debug b pc = $a
debug b pc = $b
debug b pc = $c
debug b pc = $d
debug b pc = $e
debug b pc = $f
debug b pc = $10
debug b pc = $11
debug b pc = $12
debug b pc = $13
debug b pc = $14
debug b pc = $15
debug b pc = $16
debug b all
debug b pc = $7a50 :once :trace :file {run}/level5-objs-start.ini
disk-a {disk2}
sleep 8
fire
sleep 4
fire
expect level1-read read sector sector=0x3 .*tr=0xc .*addr=0x3e
quiet level1-loaded 3
fire
sleep 2
fire
sleep 2
fire
sleep 15
